<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of New Galicia</h1><p class="st-meta">1531 CE – 1821 CE · capital Guadalajara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Spanish kingdom of western Mexico, centred on Guadalajara, created by a brutal conquest and enriched by the silver of Zacatecas.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuno-de-guzman">Nuño de Guzmán</a> led a notoriously violent campaign through western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1529-31, founding towns and naming the territory Nueva <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-galicia-and-lodomeria">Galicia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalajara-mexico">Guadalajara</a> was founded in 1532 and, after several moves, settled at its present site in 1542.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-galicia">New Galicia</a> had its own audiencia from 1548, seated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalajara-mexico">Guadalajara</a> from 1560, giving it a degree of autonomy within <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/new-spain">New Spain</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mixton-war">Mixtón War</a> of 1540-42, a major indigenous uprising, nearly ended Spanish rule there. From 1546 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zacatecas">Zacatecas</a> made the region rich and drew settlers north. Ranching and agriculture fed the mining towns.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1786 the kingdom became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/intendancy-of-guadalajara">Intendancy of Guadalajara</a>. With independence in 1821 it passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-mexican-empire">First Mexican Empire</a>, and its territory became the states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalisco">Jalisco</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayarit">Nayarit</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aguascalientes">Aguascalientes</a> and parts of others.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-new-galicia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of New Galicia" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Keepscases · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Kingdom_of_Galicia_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1531 CE – 1821 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Guadalajara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nuño de Guzmán</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nueva Galicia, New Galicia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1676&amp;focus=kingdom-of-new-galicia" aria-label="Kingdom of New Galicia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="1898 1413 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of New Galicia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2218 1669L2321 1717M2218 1669L2321 1717"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2321 1717h0M2321 1717h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2218 1669h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2218 1669h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Guadalajara. <a href="/atlas?year=1676&amp;focus=kingdom-of-new-galicia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
